New Chinese regulatory certification filings appear to confirm the battery capacities of Apple's upcoming <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max models.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/iphone-17-pro-black-feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1043676" /><br/>
According to new filings in China's C3 database, <a href="https://weibo.com/6048569942/5316883085788374">spotted</a> by the leaker known as "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/digital-chat-station/">Digital Chat Station</a>" on Weibo, the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; is seemingly rated for 4,056mAh in China and 4,288mAh in the U.S., up modestly from the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a>'s 3,988mAh and 4,252mAh. The &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max shows a bigger jump, rated for 5,391mAh in China and 5,567mAh in the U.S., compared with 4,823mAh and 5,088mAh on the &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj; Max, an increase of nearly 500mAh.<br/>
